    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44380" root="&#xA;                        هوى&#xA;                    " body-key="h1">
                        
                            1
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَوَى بِهِ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He made it to fall down:</i> see an
ex. in a verse of Ru-beh, cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِياَغٌ</span>, in
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ريغ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See 4. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَوَتْ أُذُنُهُ</span>
                        <i>His ears heard
a confused,</i> or <i>humming,</i> or <i>singing, sound.</i>
(K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَوَتْ أُمُّهُ</span> is used to express wonder;
like as when one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَاتَلَهُ ٱللّٰهُ مَا أَسْمَعَهُ</span>.
(IB, in TA, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ام</span>.)

